claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794257647722044001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c24e2c1c-bc2e-473a-9687-e12b2980a94d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"},{"link_uuid":"a37f2cef-2a43-4f0a-9388-579d792ba627","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"7341-7f22-b13a-442c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe model-upgrade task `beaten-natural-grouse` moves the production compose defaults (`infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:97-99`) and the Bedrock CloudWatch alarm dimensions (`infra/terraform/monitoring_eb6e.tf:80-135`) to `us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5`, `us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5` and `us.anthropic.claude-haiku-5-5`. The unit test `tests/unit/test_reviewbot_bedrock_cutover.py` proves the alarms name the same ids the bot invokes, but it cannot prove that Bedrock publishes metrics under exactly those `ModelId` strings. The alarms use `treat_missing_data = \"notBreaching\"` (`monitoring_eb6e.tf:42`), so a dimension that matches no published series would never page, silently.\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the upgrade change has merged and the operator has applied the terraform and redeployed the production server, run the read-only `aws cloudwatch list-metrics --namespace AWS/Bedrock --metric-name Invocations --profile frontier --region us-east-1` and compare each listed `ModelId` with the three alarm dimensions character for character. If a 5.5 id is missing from the published series, or spelled differently, file a bug linked `discovered_from` this task with the listed series and the alarm values. Reading the published series is the only check that observes what CloudWatch actually keys on; production stays read-only (applying terraform and redeploying are operator steps, not part of this task).\n\n## Scope\n\nNone: this verification changes no repository file. Evidence lives in a comment on this ticket.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The `aws cloudwatch list-metrics` output, its PST timestamp, and the per-id match result for the three 5.5 `ModelId` dimensions are recorded in a ticket comment.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","7341-7f22-b13a-442c"],["parent","9794-4336-5ed6-4561"],["relates_to","7341-7f22-b13a-442c"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Why no repository files change: the compose and alarm edits land in beaten-natural-grouse; this task only reads published CloudWatch metric series after deploy. Where output or evidence lives: a comment on ticket itchy-neutral-whooper with the list-metrics output and match result.","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"eeb7-c365-6e95-4802","ticket_type":"task","title":"Point deploy model defaults and Bedrock alarms at the 5.5 inference profiles","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["76daaf33-cf40-47b9-938d-d9bfb9c1805e","ad61fed6-5ee2-4fee-8718-e5ab9fe5406d","c24e2c1c-bc2e-473a-9687-e12b2980a94d","ee92bfa8-9ca4-4c7d-9b35-4af87a981537","1193dc8b-2eb2-4875-aaeb-b5315515ae89","a37f2cef-2a43-4f0a-9388-579d792ba627"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794260742180018002,"uuid":"3aba6bfb-0a73-4a57-8e0a-3848f4c7d84e"}